From f6b8e3ed12aa504cf19bdcaf4211898f6e347568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 03:33:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/36] tests: use TROJITA_HEADLESS_TEST instead of raw
 QTEST_GUILESS_MAIN

QTEST_GUILESS_MAIN is Qt5-only. tests/Utils/headless_test.h already
defines TROJITA_HEADLESS_TEST as the dual-Qt-safe equivalent -- Qt5
branch delegates to QTEST_GUILESS_MAIN, Qt4 branch hand-builds the
same QCoreApplication + QTest::qExec() main() -- and 26 other test
files already use it correctly. These 5 were bypassing that existing,
working convention with the raw Qt5-only macro directly. Switched to
TROJITA_HEADLESS_TEST (adding the missing include where needed);
confirmed via grep no raw QTEST_GUILESS_MAIN call sites remain outside
headless_test.h's own (correctly guarded) definition.
---
 tests/Cryptography/test_Cryptography_MessageModel.cpp | 3 ++-
 tests/Cryptography/test_Cryptography_PGP.cpp          | 3 ++-
 tests/Imap/test_Imap_Parser_write.cpp                 | 3 ++-
 tests/Misc/test_Formatting.cpp                        | 3 ++-
 tests/Misc/test_prettySize.cpp                        | 3 ++-
 5 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

